**Bug fixed.** The issue was on line 43 of `/Users/tijs/projects/local-model-bench/runner/runs/tmpktxmnu75/run/src/sim.ts`:

- **Before:** `if (foodSurplus >= 0)` — population grew even when production equals consumption (foodSurplus = 0)
- **After:** `if (foodSurplus > 0)` — population now only grows when there's an actual surplus (foodSurplus > 0)

This ensures settlements that are just barely breaking even no longer see population growth each turn. Population will only increase when there's genuine excess food production beyond what the current population consumes.


